sechost, services: service object security (QueryServiceObjectSecurity/SetServiceObjectSecurity).
Both were stubs (an empty DACL / ignored writes; the service manager returned
ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED). Now the service manager stores the descriptor like
Windows in Services\<name>\Security ("Security", self-relative), merges the parts
the caller passes, returns only the requested parts, and uses Windows' default
service DACL when none is stored; sechost forwards both calls over svcctl.
Epic Games' updater grants users the right to start its service and checks that
grant ("Service has not been granted with correct permissions"); without it the
launcher could not update itself.

